//? Title: Petrick: actual expansion and absorption
//? Subtitle: Canonical C++ producers, original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Each clause lists alternative implicant ids that cover one required minterm.
Distributive expansion forms candidate id sets; absorption discards duplicates
and supersets. The final smallest-cardinality surviving terms are all
minimum-count covers. Literal costs are not minimised here. An empty chart has
the identity empty cover; an empty clause is unsatisfiable. Exponential
intermediate growth remains possible and is explicitly limited. The original
three-variable cyclic Quine-McCluskey chart is retained; no external dataset is
appropriate.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

Each clause lists alternative implicant ids that cover one required minterm.
Distributive expansion forms candidate id sets; absorption discards duplicates
and supersets. The final smallest-cardinality surviving terms are all
minimum-count covers. Literal costs are not minimised here. An empty chart has
the identity empty cover; an empty clause is unsatisfiable. Exponential
intermediate growth remains possible and is explicitly limited. The original
three-variable cyclic Quine-McCluskey chart is retained; no external dataset is
appropriate.

$$ P=\prod_{i}\left(\sum_{j\in C_i}p_j\right),\qquad X+XY=X. $$

The empty product is true and corresponds to the empty cover; an empty sum is
false and makes the chart uncoverable.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native diagram use the same producing run. Captured records own
their values; the report does not reconstruct the algorithm.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/petrick_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::petrick_trace({{0, 1}, {1, 2}});
    std::print("| clause | actual candidates | absorbed | actual surviving terms |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | " "--- |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.stages)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | `{}` |\n", r.clause, r.generated,
                   r.absorbed, r.terms);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual distributed candidates\n{}", t.generated));
    d.node("n1", {8, 0},
           std::format("Actual surviving terms\n{}", t.stages.back().terms));
    d.node("n2", {16, 0},
           std::format("Actual minimum-count covers\n{}",
                       t.result.minimal_covers));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/petrick_tiny.svg");
}
```
